{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מבלתי", :translit "mibli", :gloss "from lack of / because not"} {:he "מבלתי יכולת ה'", :translit "mibli ycholet Hashem", :gloss "because the LORD was not able"} {:he "ותזנו אל בני אשור מבלתי שבעתך", :translit "vatiznu el bnei ashur mibli sovatecha", :gloss "and you played the harlot with the children of Assyria because you were not sated"} {:he "תועבות ירושלים", :translit "to'avot Yerushalayim", :gloss "abominations of Jerusalem"} {:he "עונות ישראל", :translit "avonot Yisrael", :gloss "iniquities of Israel"} {:he "יד חזקה", :translit "yad chazakah", :gloss "strong hand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מבלתי יכולת ה'" "ותזנו אל בני אשור מבלתי שבעתך"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'מבלתי יכולת ה׳' appears in Numbers 14:16, where Moses warns God that if He destroys Israel the nations will say He lacked the power to bring them into the land. The parallel occurrence in Ezekiel 16:28 uses 'מבלתי שבעתך' for Jerusalem's insatiable turn to Assyria, which Ezekiel 16:2 frames as the abominations of Jerusalem. Ba'al HaTurim reads the shared word as linking Israel's complaint in the wilderness to Jerusalem's later sin, so that the accumulated iniquities overwhelm the attribute of 'יד חזקה' (Exodus 13:3, Deuteronomy 5:15).", :sources ["Numbers 14:16" "Ezekiel 16:28" "Ezekiel 16:2" "Exodus 13:3" "Deuteronomy 5:15"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וישחטם במדבר", :translit "vayishchatem bamidbar", :gloss "and He will slaughter them in the wilderness"} {:he "שחוטה", :translit "shchutah", :gloss "slaughtered [feminine]"} {:he "החי\"ת", :translit "ha'cheit", :gloss "the letter chet"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "החית", :b "שמונה בריתות בכלל ושמונה בריתות בפרט"}], :frame {:text "The feminine form 'ונשחטה' with its chet (ח) links to the promise 'ושחטת' in Exodus 24:8, where Moses sprinkled the blood of the covenant, and to the eight covenants cut over the Torah. Ba'al HaTurim reads the word's form as signaling that Israel's transgression of that covenant in Numbers 14:34–35 invited the angels of destruction, paralleling the 'מלאך המשחית' dispatched in 2 Samuel 24:16.", :sources ["Exodus 24:8" "Numbers 14:34-35" "2 Samuel 24:16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מבלתי יכולת ה'" "ותזנו אל בני אשור מבלתי שבעתך"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מבלתי יכולת ה'", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ותזנו אל בני אשור מבלתי שבעתך", :refs ["Ezekiel 16:28"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "החית", :a-value 423, :b "שמונה בריתות בכלל ושמונה בריתות בפרט", :b-value 3217, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:29:01.853764277Z", :model "glm-5.2"}